CAVECODE SPEC — BASIC SWAP (ARC-HM-001)
Category: haze-maze
Engine: Match-3 Swap
Version: 1.1

============================================================
🪨 BLOCK 1 — IDENTITY
------------------------------------------------------------
Title: Haze Maze — Basic Swap
Game ID: ARC-HM-001
Category: haze-maze
Genre: match-3 swap
One-Liner: Swap tiles to form matches. Tiles clear, new ones fall.
(LOCKED)

============================================================
🎮 BLOCK 2 — CORE LOOP SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------
Each tick:
  - Start with no pre-existing matches and at least one legal swap.
  - Wait for player input (select tile A → select tile B).
  - Ignore input after level win/loss until replay or next level.
  - Each adjacent swap attempt costs one move, including invalid swaps.
  - If adjacent, attempt swap.
  - If swap creates a match → resolve matches → gravity → refill.
  - If no match created → swap back (invalid swap).
  - After cascades settle, regenerate any dead board without extra move/score cost.
  - Restart clears selection, score, counters and the result modal.
Loop is event-driven, not time-driven.
(LOCKED)

============================================================
🕹️ BLOCK 3 — INPUT / CONTROLS
------------------------------------------------------------
Desktop:
  - Click tile 1, then click tile 2.
Mobile:
  - Tap tile 1, then tap tile 2.
Optional drag gesture: detect direction to pick adjacent tile.
(LOCKED)

============================================================
📈 BLOCK 4 — SCORING / PROGRESSION
------------------------------------------------------------
Each matched group: length * 10 points, plus 40 per tile beyond three.
Cascade multiplier: 1 + cascadeIndex * 0.25 (first clear uses 1.0).
Four-tile groups create row/column specials; five or more create bombs.
Special tiles activate when included in a clear.
Five levels (target score / moves): 800/18, 1700/22, 2600/26, 3600/28, 4800/30.
Score resets each level. Reach target to win; exhaust moves first to lose.
Final level can be replayed. Sound provides match, invalid-swap and result feedback.
(LOCKED)

============================================================
🎚️ BLOCK 5 — TUNING KNOBS (HUMAN EDIT ZONE)
------------------------------------------------------------
gridRows: 8
gridCols: 8
tileTypes: 5          # Number of different colored tiles
clearScore: 10
extraMatchBonus: 4   # multiplied by clearScore for each tile beyond three
chainStep: 0.25
gravityEnabled: true
refillMode: "top-down"   # drop new tiles from above
matchLength: 3
(PENCIL — safe to modify)

